# Fabriq verbose stream capture (standard deployment, default ON).
#
# Presence of this file enables cmdlet.verbose telemetry events:
#   - Invoke-SafeCommand wraps each module run with $VerbosePreference='Continue'
#     and a 4>&1 stream redirect.
#   - Built-in cmdlet verbose output (Set-ItemProperty / Set-NetAdapterBinding /
#     Rename-Computer / etc.) is captured as cmdlet.verbose events in the
#     module envelope JSONL.
#   - Output is local-only: log_uploader excludes logs/telemetry/.
#
# To opt out: delete this file. fabriq will start in standard mode with
# verbose capture inactive (no PSDefaultParameterValues mutation, no
# stream redirect overhead).
#
# This file's contents are not parsed; only its presence matters.
# See dev/TELEMETRY_INTERNAL.md §6.7 for the full schema and trade-offs.
